{title: My Faith Looks Up to Thee}
{artist: Ray Palmer / Lowell Mason}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: D}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: my-faith-looks-up-to-thee.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (My_Faith_Looks_Up_To_Thee-Olivet) and the Cyber Hymnal score (95% of syllables agree)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]My faith looks [A]up to [D]Thee,
[A7]Thou Lamb of Calvary, [D]Sa[E7]vior di[A7]vine!
[D]Now hear me while I pray, take all my guilt away,
[Bm]O [A]let me [D]from this day be [Em]whol[A7]ly [D]Thine!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]May Thy rich [A]grace im[D]part
[A7]Strength to my fainting heart, [D]my [E7]zeal in[A7]spire!
[D]As Thou hast died for me, O may my love to Thee,
[Bm]Pure [A]warm, and [D]changeless be, a [Em]liv[A7]ing [D]fire!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]While life’s dark [A]maze I [D]tread,
[A7]And griefs around me spread, [D]be [E7]Thou my [A7]guide;
[D]Bid darkness turn to day, wipe sorrow’s tears away,
[Bm]Nor [A]let me [D]ever stray from [Em]Thee [A7]a[D]side.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]When ends life's [A]transient [D]dream,
[A7]When death's cold sullen stream [D]ov[E7]er me [A7]roll;
[D]Blest Savior, then in love, fear and distrust remove;
[Bm]O [A]bear me [D]safe above, a [Em]ran[A7]somed [D]soul!
{end_of_verse}
